<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Forrest</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1847">1847</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sir John Forrest</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Forrest was an Australian explorer, surveyor and politician who crossed the western deserts in the 1870s. When Western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> gained responsible government in 1890 he became its first premier, serving until 1901 through the gold rushes at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coolgardie">Coolgardie</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalgoorlie">Kalgoorlie</a>. He then entered the new federal parliament and served in several Commonwealth ministries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-forrest.jpg" alt="John Forrest" width="320" height="523" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Emanuel Phillips Fox (1865–1915) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Right_Honourable_Sir_John_Forrest.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
